{
    "word": "physiognomy",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                "word": "physiognomy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c1ca345c-7cb0-416a-a822-c3c096bf29d5",
                        "entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "physiognomies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "77814328-241b-3ad5-939c-f3775cebc0ff",
                        "entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The art or pseudoscience of deducing the predominant temper and other characteristic qualities of the mind from the outward appearance, especially from the features of the face."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "922543e4-f81e-4272-8021-cf420d1f3b51",
                                "sense_id": "77814328-241b-3ad5-939c-f3775cebc0ff",
                                "text": "Known still less than Della Porta is the figure of Camillo Baldi, an early-seventeenth-century Bolognese physician and university professor who advanced the discussion from the study of physiognomy and skull sizes to the study of characteriology based on writing. I am still not sure what to make of this treatise on onychomancy, that is, divining by observing the fingernails, except that he accounted for the practice as an example of the acute application of observational technique to the signs and symbols left by intelligent nature for humans to decipher in view of some benefit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37f026cb-da9a-4619-be2b-74733845fb2f",
                                "sense_id": "77814328-241b-3ad5-939c-f3775cebc0ff",
                                "text": "During a period of peak popularity in the 19ᵗʰ Century, the field of physiognomy became more sinister and racist than its quirky manifestation during the time of ancient Greeks."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "73384e34-b881-3ed1-8093-466de8f2f48d",
                        "entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The face or countenance, with respect to the temper of the mind; particular configuration, cast, or expression of countenance, as denoting character."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9d34627-bd86-4416-a488-445ffb2ccf72",
                                "sense_id": "73384e34-b881-3ed1-8093-466de8f2f48d",
                                "text": "Faith ſir a has an Engliſh maine, but his fiſnomie is more hotter in France then there."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40ed4db9-f214-4670-b36f-daea4cf56fb2",
                                "sense_id": "73384e34-b881-3ed1-8093-466de8f2f48d",
                                "text": "The Negro transported into the same countries has also undergone remarkable changes. His colour has paled, his features have improved, and his physiognomy is altered. “In the space of 150 years,” says M. Elisée Reclus, “they have passed a good fourth of the distance which separates them from the whites, as far as external appearance goes.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ce33b74a-a75d-37fb-a867-2ffc820659c3",
                        "entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The art of telling fortunes by inspection of the features."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e09fc647-459d-30a0-9ca8-5017ee6db26a",
                        "entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The general appearance or aspect of a thing, without reference to its scientific characteristics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "33be223a-d66f-4539-bfaa-4f1b16b90224",
                                "sense_id": "e09fc647-459d-30a0-9ca8-5017ee6db26a",
                                "text": "the physiognomy of a plant; of a meteor"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7e2d286-6ade-446d-ad91-f890ed2446b3",
                                "sense_id": "e09fc647-459d-30a0-9ca8-5017ee6db26a",
                                "text": "According to artists, the lion is the most difficult of all animals to paint, on account of the prodigious mobility of his physiognomy. Rosa Bonheur was able, thanks to her inimitable art, to catch and reproduce the fugitive facial expressions of the kingly beast [...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5871e7a3-1970-4344-b80f-f7d88c45a6f2",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "source_sense_description": "art or pseudoscience of deducing the character or personality from the bodily appearance",
                        "target_lang_word": "fyziognomie",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "58bcb730-f639-4797-b586-0ebd1862f679",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "source_sense_description": "art or pseudoscience of deducing the character or personality from the bodily appearance",
                        "target_lang_word": "physiognomonie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "physiognomonie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8226f15f-a57e-318d-ab9b-347b0f4b9997",
                                        "entry_id": "4e5f79c3-70ca-3ba6-985a-431b035072a3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Étude du caractère à partir des traits du visage → voir physionomie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec84c2f8-4bd0-480e-a2bb-420883e792f3",
                                                "sense_id": "8226f15f-a57e-318d-ab9b-347b0f4b9997",
                                                "text": "La guerre permettait de réaffirmer et de mettre en pratique les stéréotypes tenaces qui voulaient que « l’habileté native » du Vietnamien le destine au travail d’usine ; les circulaires de la Direction des troupes coloniales constituent de véritables traités de physiognomonie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5ac9b10-e549-4844-b9b7-e870483d22da",
                                                "sense_id": "8226f15f-a57e-318d-ab9b-347b0f4b9997",
                                                "text": "Jadis, la passion de la physiognomonie eût peut-être poussé un Gall à disséquer les cerveaux de champions d’échecs d’une telle espèce pour voir si la matière grise de pareils génies ne présentait pas une circonvolution particulière qui la distinguât des autres, une sorte de muscle ou de bosse des échecs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f94800c-6387-4b99-85c1-0ab57a8f8787",
                                                "sense_id": "8226f15f-a57e-318d-ab9b-347b0f4b9997",
                                                "text": "Chaque homme a une science immédiate et intuitive de la physionomie, et une pathognomonique à lui ; cependant les uns saisissent plus facilement que les autres cette signatura rerum. Mais une connaissance in abstractos de la physiognomonie ne peut ni constituer une science, ni s’enseigner comme telle ; car les nuances en sont si fines, que le concept ne peut descendre jusqu’à elles. (…) Je suis, par conséquent, d’avis que la physiognomonie ne peut aller bien loin, si elle veut rester sûre ; elle doit se borner à formuler quelques règles très générales, par exemple : c’est dans le front et dans l’œil que réside l’intelligence ; c’est dans la bouche et dans la partie inférieure du visage que se trahissent et le caractère et les manifestations du vouloir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e845d12-3e2a-4bd7-9487-a2283bd3d4e2",
                                                "sense_id": "8226f15f-a57e-318d-ab9b-347b0f4b9997",
                                                "text": "Son menton et le bas de son visage étaient un peu gras, dans l’acception que les peintres donnent à ce mot, et cette forme épaisse est, suivant les lois impitoyables de la physiognomonie, l’indice d'une violence quasi morbide dans la passion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11bb16e8-89ac-3caa-a2d7-170064e1bf20",
                                        "entry_id": "4e5f79c3-70ca-3ba6-985a-431b035072a3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Traité qui a cette matière pour sujet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0f9ced3-9a91-45a0-bd19-75f66bcbbf36",
                                                "sense_id": "11bb16e8-89ac-3caa-a2d7-170064e1bf20",
                                                "text": "J’imaginais un vieux bonhomme, je ne sais pas pourquoi, peut-être le prénom Hubert. […]. En fait, Hubert Haddad a la tête d’un type qui a roulé sa bosse, mais rien qui l’apparente à Hubert Reeves, il va falloir que je révise ma physiognomonie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb91b48e-8982-4e9d-a715-de0d2af5ee21",
                                                "sense_id": "11bb16e8-89ac-3caa-a2d7-170064e1bf20",
                                                "text": "La Physiognomonie de Lavater a créé une véritable science, qui a enfin pris place parmi les connaissances humaines ; car, si, d’abord, quelques doutes, quelques plaisanteries accueillirent l’apparition de ce livre, depuis, le célèbre docteur Gall vint par sa belle théorie du crâne, achever et compléter le système du Suisse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "95236430-e306-4e1c-a15c-7a495a847338",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "source_sense_description": "art or pseudoscience of deducing the character or personality from the bodily appearance",
                        "target_lang_word": "Physiognomik",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Physiognomik",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd3d0a0d-7866-391c-9d60-8d7f2eaba330",
                                        "entry_id": "7af57980-079c-3abe-8515-01ef4c6974ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Disziplin, die versucht, vom Aussehen einer Person auf ihre Eigenschaften zu schließen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a76a4ea-b75d-4580-b305-a51938345b40",
                                                "sense_id": "fd3d0a0d-7866-391c-9d60-8d7f2eaba330",
                                                "text": "„Vom männlichen Nachwuchs habe ich nur ihren Erstgeborenen genauer betrachtet und fand sein Gesicht unheilverkündend, trotz der gegenteiligen Meinung des Abate Testagrossa, der sich auch auf dem Gebiet der Physiognomik als Kenner fühlte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ea61b17b-940d-4ba7-9a2e-dfdb5797dd71",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "source_sense_description": "art or pseudoscience of deducing the character or personality from the bodily appearance",
                        "target_lang_word": "физионо́мика",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "физионо́мика",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9646de72-b4f3-3cda-86c3-6649c83491ec",
                                        "entry_id": "57beb6c2-396a-333e-af40-ab2e67f0b55b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "истор. химерическое искусство разгадывать по лицу и телу свойства и качества человека"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d837e4b8-dc69-4d3d-b169-d93a1cfb0c51",
                                                "sense_id": "9646de72-b4f3-3cda-86c3-6649c83491ec",
                                                "text": "Как и жизнь отдельного индивида, жизнь народа есть некое конкретное, целостное единство, воспринимаемое своего рода «физиономикой», тою «художественной практикой духовного портретирования», о котором хорошо говорил Шпенглер."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fb9c70d-94f8-4397-a634-250494e83ea2",
                                                "sense_id": "9646de72-b4f3-3cda-86c3-6649c83491ec",
                                                "text": "Старик кроме мистицизма был заражен ещё и лафатеровой физиономикой."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cdb26bf6-bde8-45a1-9501-798f0a14fea8",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
                        "source_sense_description": "art or pseudoscience of deducing the character or personality from the bodily appearance",
                        "target_lang_word": "физиогно́мика",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "физиогно́мика",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2fbea537-39c3-3086-a853-56823badbf52",
                                        "entry_id": "5836d474-c51a-32e4-95e6-8d220aec2196",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "устар. то же, что физиономика; химерическое искусство определять характер и внутренние качества человека по его внешности и особенно по лицу"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bd18443-b138-4aea-995e-29b2e60124e1",
                                                "sense_id": "2fbea537-39c3-3086-a853-56823badbf52",
                                                "text": "Было время когда изучением корреляций между характером и построением головы, в особенности лица, занималась так называемая физиогномика, считавшаяся до известной степени особой наукой."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d659b11b-b7c0-44d0-8a6b-bf7bf3d7067f",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3bfabc2-eba5-3611-b014-15b00d6d703f",
